# Etrata, Deadly Fugitive (1/4 deathtouch Vampire Assassin): "Whenever an Assassin you control deals combat damage to an opponent, cloak the top card of that player's library." (CR 510.2, 603.2, 701.58a.)
# Each Assassin has its own trigger. On turn 5 Etrata and Merfolk Assassin (an Assassin as well) and Grizzly Bears (not one) attack Bot2, who has no creatures: Etrata's and the Merfolk's damage trigger twice, so the
# top two cards of Bot2's library are cloaked under Bot1's control, in the order they were on top (Grizzly Bears, then Llanowar Elves), face-down 2/2 creatures with ward {2}. The Bears' damage cloaks nothing.
# Bot2 loses 1 + 1 + 2 = 4 life, and has 20 cards, 7 in hand and 2 drawn by turn 5, so 11 left, and two are cloaked, leaving 9.

